From 0470c693f7379d0ec629fdac5a12a4add33d3a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Travis Cole <11240+kelp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:58:13 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] eject: card_away stops More like this's request

ringnav_usbmode called similar_stop (more-like-this); eject-card moved
its stops into card_away, so the call moves there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DaXZzN3FY6RrXiA6e34J2b
---
 patch/eject.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/patch/eject.c b/patch/eject.c
index 0231bb27..b6663f07 100644
--- a/patch/eject.c
+++ b/patch/eject.c
@@ -17,12 +17,14 @@ extern void eject_sync(void);
 
 /* The jobs that write to the card or keep its files open, each stopped: the card apps (they run
  * from /tmp: addon.c), Tidal's downloads (tidal.c), Download Album Lyrics' job, playlist art's
- * worker and the song durations' (durations.c). USB Storage (navigation.c ringnav_usbmode) and
+ * worker and the song durations' (durations.c); More like this's request stops, so no mix of the
+ * card's songs plays (similar.c). USB Storage (navigation.c ringnav_usbmode) and
  * Eject Card. */
 void card_away(void) {
     tidal_card_away();
     addon_card_away();
     album_lyrics_stop();
+    similar_stop();
     playlist_art_stop();
     durations_shutdown(0);
 }
